.git
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo

dataset
notebooks
tests
mlruns_snapshot

data/analytics
data/processed

# Exclude reports/ by default, but api/main.py and ensemble.py read a
# handful of these CSVs at request time (interval calibration/coverage
# diagnostics, and headline's dynamic ensemble weight source) -- keep those
# specific files uploaded to Cloud Build so the Docker build (which mirrors
# this same allowlist in .dockerignore) can include them. Use reports/*
# (not a bare "reports") so the negations below actually take effect.
reports/*
!reports/model_interval_coverage.csv
!reports/model_interval_calibration_factors.csv
!reports/model_interval_calibration_validation.csv
!reports/model_interval_coverage_trimmed_mean.csv
!reports/model_interval_calibration_factors_trimmed_mean.csv
!reports/model_interval_calibration_validation_trimmed_mean.csv
!reports/model_comparison_elastic_net.csv

# Deliberately NOT ignoring mlruns/ or data/curated/, unlike .gitignore --
# the Cloud Run image is built from a local checkout that bakes in the
# current local MLflow run history (see README's "API, Dashboard, And
# Deployment" section). gcloud builds submit falls back to .gitignore's
# rules when no .gcloudignore is present, which would silently drop
# mlruns/ from the uploaded build context and break `COPY mlruns mlruns`
# in the Dockerfile.
